                    sum_r4_good:            `Defended on outcome, differentiated, committed dates.`,
                    sum_r4_weak:            `Folded on scope, price or timeline under pressure.`,

                    insight_won:            `You won the renewal: a backward-designed program that fixes the real problem, priced above the 25% floor and under the ceiling, deliverable in 8 weeks. The audition cohort earns the $3.2M relationship.`,
                    insight_lossmaking:     `You won the cohort and lost money: a margin below the floor means this engagement doesn't fund the unit. A loss-making audition is a fragile foundation for a five-year renewal.`,
                    insight_generic:        `The program felt generic. Reused modules, substituted faculty or a thin differentiation argument told the CHRO it wasn't built for her — and a generic cohort loses the audition regardless of price.`,
                    insight_overbudget:     `You priced above the $280K ceiling. Whatever the design, a number over the client's stated budget loses credibility before the value argument is even heard.`,
                    insight_belowfloor:     `Your contribution margin fell below the 25% floor. You cut price where you should have cut cost — the won engagement doesn't pay for the bespoke work you promised.`,
                    insight_undeliverable:  `Deliverability is low: you broke the 4-day cap, ignored faculty lead-times, or over-promised the 8-week window. A program you can't actually launch on time fails the audition at delivery.`,
                    insight_lowfit:         `Client fit stayed low — the program didn't feel built for MeridianHealth. The “custom” in custom cohort is what the renewal is paying for; without it you're competing on price alone.`,
                    insight_audition:       `This is the audition won the right way: genuine fit, a healthy margin and a realistic timeline moving together. A thinner-but-real first cohort that earns a multi-year relationship is worth far more than a fat one-off.`,

                    hint_belowfloor:        `Your margin is below the 25% floor — the cohort doesn't fund the unit. Cut cost (logistics, faculty mix) or add justified value, rather than cutting price further.`,
